# Boyue Likebook Alita (K103) - Android 8.1 SELinux Bypass Patch
# Architecture: ARM64 (aarch64)
# Target file: /init (in boot.img ramdisk)

--- File Offset 0x0000d130 (Virtual Address 0x0040d130) ---

ORIGINAL (AOSP init enforces SELinux):
  File offset: 0xd130
  Hex bytes:   71 04 00 35
  Disassembly: cbnz w0, 0x40dcdc   ; PLOG(FATAL) << "Failed to set enforce mode"

PATCHED (Direct branch to bypass enforcing call):
  File offset: 0xd130
  Hex bytes:   06 00 00 14
  Disassembly: b    0x40d148       ; Skip selinux_set_enforce(1) completely

Explanation:
  By default in the Likebook kernel cmdline, androidboot.selinux=permissive is passed.
  During stage 2 of init, Android executes selinux_set_enforce(1) to lock SELinux into Enforcing.
  Bypassing this call leaves the kernel in its natural Permissive state, permitting domain transitions,
  unprivileged su execution, and root filesystem read/write.
